# ScholarScribe. Line-ending and diff policy (v0.1 work order A1).
#
# Goal: hash-checked and byte-embedded files must be byte-identical on
# every OS. LF is forced for everything the Rust build embeds or hashes
# (include_str!/include_bytes! assets, frozen fixtures, the golden set,
# the word-addin client) so Windows checkouts cannot produce CRLF
# variants that break checksum or "dist matches source" gates.
# Nothing is renormalized retroactively: rules apply to the named paths.

# Frozen evaluation / golden fixtures (hash-checked by tests).
src-tauri/tests/assist/*.json text eol=lf
src-tauri/tests/eval/*.jsonl text eol=lf
src-tauri/tests/eval/*.md text eol=lf
src-tauri/fixtures/** text eol=lf

# Add-in client: served byte-for-byte by the listener and embedded in
# the binary (include_str!). The manifest is fetched by Word.
word-addin/dist/** text eol=lf
word-addin/src/** text eol=lf
word-addin/*.json text eol=lf

# Embedded reference/network surfaces that CI compares as text.
src/lib/references.json text eol=lf
docs/NETWORK_SURFACE.json text eol=lf

# Release-time artifact that must not churn by platform.
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md text eol=lf

# Icons are binary; never let git touch them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
